 {
  "date": "2026-10-24",
  "title": "2025年6月 第3套 · 南水北调",
  "zh": "自古以来，中国的水资源北缺南丰，分布极不均衡。为了有效解决北方严重缺水问题，中国政府实施了南水北调工程（the South-to-North Water Diversion Project）。这是一项跨区域配置水资源的宏大水利工程。历经数十年的规划与筹备，工程于 2002 年开工建设，分为东、中、西三条线路，总长 4350 公里，惠及人口将超过 4 亿。自 2014 年通水以来，工程向北方调水累计已超 500 亿立方米，为北方地区的人民提供了可靠的水资源，同时也极大地改善了这一地区的生态环境，促进了经济的可持续健康发展。",
  "ref": "Since ancient times China's water resources have been scarce in the north and abundant in the south, with an extremely uneven distribution. To effectively solve the serious water shortage in the north, the Chinese government has carried out the South-to-North Water Diversion Project. It is a huge water conservancy project that allocates water resources across regions. After decades of planning and preparation, construction began in 2002. The project consists of three routes—east, middle and west—with a total length of 4,350 kilometres, and will benefit more than 400 million people. Since water began flowing in 2014, more than 50 billion cubic metres have been diverted to the north, providing reliable water resources for the people there, greatly improving the ecological environment of the region and promoting sustainable and sound economic development."
 },
